# Key Takeaways

This lab demonstrates why blacklist-based filtering is unreliable.

Removing dangerous substrings without validating the final canonical path leaves applications vulnerable to traversal bypass techniques.

The proper defense is not to sanitize traversal sequences but to ensure that the resolved path always remains within an authorized directory.
